<h2>Scope of the Tutorial</h2>

<p>This tutorial will show you how to write assembly language programs on t=
he x86-64 architecture.

</p><p>You will write both (1) standalone programs and (2) programs that in=
tegrate with C.

</p><p>Don=E2=80=99t worry, we won=E2=80=99t get too fancy.

</p><h2>Your First Program</h2>

<p>Before learning any details, let=E2=80=99s make sure you can type in and=
 run programs.

</p><p>Make sure both nasm and gcc are installed. Save one of the following=
 programs as <strong>hello.asm</strong>, depending on your machine platform=
. Then run the program according to the given instructions.

</p><p>If you are on a Linux-based OS:

