<h2>Defining Data and Reserving Space</h2>

<p>These examples come from <a href=3D"https://www.nasm.us/xdoc/2.15.05/htm=
l/nasmdoc3.html">Chapter 3 of the docs</a>. To place data in memory:

</p><pre class=3D"prettyprint lang-asm"><span class=3D"pln">&nbsp; &nbsp; &=
nbsp; db &nbsp; &nbsp;0x55 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;=
 &nbsp;</span><span class=3D"com">; just the byte 0x55</span><span class=3D=
"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; db &nbsp; &nbsp;0x55,0x56,0x57 &nbsp; &nbsp;=
 &nbsp;</span><span class=3D"com">; three bytes in succession</span><span c=
lass=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; db &nbsp; &nbsp;'a',0x55 &nbsp; &nbsp=
; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span class=3D"com">; character constan=
ts are OK</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; db &nbsp; &nbs=
p;'hello',13,10,'$' &nbsp; </span><span class=3D"com">; so are string const=
ants</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dw &nbsp; &nbsp;0x1=
234 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span class=3D"c=
om">; 0x34 0x12</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dw &nbsp=
; &nbsp;'a' &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span>=
<span class=3D"com">; 0x61 0x00 (it's just a number)</span><span class=3D"p=
ln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dw &nbsp; &nbsp;'ab' &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbs=
p; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span class=3D"com">; 0x61 0x62 (chara=
cter constant)</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dw &nbsp;=
 &nbsp;'abc' &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span =
class=3D"com">; 0x61 0x62 0x63 0x00 (string)</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>=
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dd &nbsp; &nbsp;0x12345678 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;=
 &nbsp;</span><span class=3D"com">; 0x78 0x56 0x34 0x12</span><span class=
=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dd &nbsp; &nbsp;1.234567e20 &nbsp; &nbsp;=
 &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span class=3D"com">; floating-point constant</span><=
span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dq &nbsp; &nbsp;0x123456789abcd=
ef0 &nbsp;</span><span class=3D"com">; eight byte constant</span><span clas=
s=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dq &nbsp; &nbsp;1.234567e20 &nbsp; &nbsp=
; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span class=3D"com">; double-precision float</span><=
span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; dt &nbsp; &nbsp;1.234567e20 &nb=
sp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span class=3D"com">; extended-precision fl=
oat</span></pre>
<p>There are other forms; check the NASM docs. Later.

</p><p>To reserve space (without initializing), you can use the following p=
seudo instructions. They
should go in a section called <code>.bss</code> (you'll get an error if you=
 try to use them in
a <code>.text</code> section):

</p><pre class=3D"prettyprint lang-asm"><span class=3D"pln">buffer: &nbsp; =
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; resb &nbsp; &nbsp;64 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp=
; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span><span class=3D"com">; reserve 64 bytes</span><span cl=
ass=3D"pln"><br>wordvar: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;resw &nbsp; &nbsp;1 &nb=
sp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span><span class=3D"com">; =
reserve a word</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>realarray: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp=
;resq &nbsp; &nbsp;10 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</spa=
n><span class=3D"com">; array of ten reals</span></pre>

<h2>Another Example</h2>

<p>Here=E2=80=99s a macOS program to study:

</p><div class=3D"filename"><span>triangle.asm</span></div><pre><code class=
=3D"language-x86asm hljs" data-highlighted=3D"yes"><span class=3D"hljs-comm=
ent">; --------------------------------------------------------------------=
--------------------</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; This is an macOS console program that writes=
 a little triangle of asterisks to standard</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; output. Runs on macOS only.</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;     nasm -fmacho64 triangle.asm &amp;&amp; g=
cc hola.o &amp;&amp; ./a.out</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; --------------------------------------------=
--------------------------------------------</span>

          <span class=3D"hljs-meta">global</span>    start
          <span class=3D"hljs-meta">section</span>   .text
<span class=3D"hljs-symbol">start:</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">rdx</span>, output             <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; rd=
x holds address of next byte to write</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">r8</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>                 =
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; initial line length</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">r9</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">0</span>                 =
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; number of stars written on line so far</sp=
an>
<span class=3D"hljs-symbol">line:</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">byte</span> [<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">rdx</span>], <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-string">'*'</span>         <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; write=
 single star</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">inc</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">rdx</span>                     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; ad=
vance pointer to next cell to write</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">inc</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">r9</span>                      <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; "c=
ount" number so far on line</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cmp</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">r9</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">r8</span>              =
    <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; did we reach the number of stars for thi=
s line?</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">jne</span>       line               =
     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; not yet, keep writing on this line</spa=
n>
<span class=3D"hljs-symbol">lineDone:</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">byte</span> [<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">rdx</span>], <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-number">10</span>          <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; write=
 a new line char</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">inc</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">rdx</span>                     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; an=
d move pointer to where next char goes</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">inc</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">r8</span>                      <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; ne=
xt line will be one char longer</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">r9</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">0</span>                 =
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; reset count of stars written on this line<=
/span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cmp</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">r8</span>, maxlines            <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; wa=
it, did we already finish the last line?</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">jng</span>       line               =
     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; if not, begin writing this line</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-symbol">done:</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">0x02000004</span>       =
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; system call for write</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">rdi</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>                =
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; file handle 1 is stdout</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">rsi</span>, output             <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; ad=
dress of string to output</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">rdx</span>, dataSize           <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; nu=
mber of bytes</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">syscall</span>                      =
     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; invoke operating system to do the write=
</span>
          <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>       <span class=3D"hljs=
-built_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">0x02000001</span>       =
  <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; system call for exit</span>
