<h2>Mixing C and Assembly Language</h2>

<p>This program is just a simple function that takes in three
integer parameters and returns the maximum value.

</p><div class=3D"filename"><span>maxofthree.asm</span></div><pre><code cla=
ss=3D"language-x86asm hljs" data-highlighted=3D"yes"><span class=3D"hljs-co=
mment">; ------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----------</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; A 64-bit function that returns the maximum v=
alue of its three 64-bit integer</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; arguments.  The function has signature:</spa=
n>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;   int64_t maxofthree(int64_t x, int64_t y, i=
nt64_t z)</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; Note that the parameters have already been p=
assed in rdi, rsi, and rdx.  We</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; just have to return the value in rax.</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; --------------------------------------------=
---------------------------------</span>

        <span class=3D"hljs-meta">global</span>  maxofthree
        <span class=3D"hljs-meta">section</span> .text
<span class=3D"hljs-symbol">maxofthree:</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>     <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">rdi</span>                =
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; result (rax) initially holds x</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cmp</span>     <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">rsi</span>                =
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; is x less than y?</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cmovl</span>   <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">rsi</span>                =
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; if so, set result to y</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cmp</span>     <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">rdx</span>                =
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; is max(x,y) less than z?</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cmovl</span>   <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">rdx</span>                =
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; if so, set result to z</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ret</span>                            =
 <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; the max will be in rax</span>
</code></pre>
<p>Here is a C program that calls the assembly language function.

</p><div class=3D"filename"><span>callmaxofthree.c</span></div><pre><code c=
lass=3D"language-c hljs" data-highlighted=3D"yes"><span class=3D"hljs-comme=
nt">/*
 * A small program that illustrates how to call the maxofthree function we =
wrote in
 * assembly language.
 */</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-meta">#<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">include</span> <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span>
<span class=3D"hljs-meta">#<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">include</span> <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">&lt;inttypes.h&gt;</span></span>

<span class=3D"hljs-type">int64_t</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function=
_">maxofthree</span><span class=3D"hljs-params">(<span class=3D"hljs-type">=
int64_t</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-type">int64_t</span>, <span class=3D"hl=
js-type">int64_t</span>)</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-type">int</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">m=
ain</span><span class=3D"hljs-params">()</span> {
    <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">printf</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-string"=
>"%ld\n"</span>, maxofthree(<span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>, <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-number">-4</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">-7</span>));
    <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">printf</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-string"=
>"%ld\n"</span>, maxofthree(<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-number">-6</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>));
    <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">printf</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-string"=
>"%ld\n"</span>, maxofthree(<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-number">3</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>));
    <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">printf</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-string"=
>"%ld\n"</span>, maxofthree(<span class=3D"hljs-number">-2</span>, <span cl=
ass=3D"hljs-number">4</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">3</span>));
    <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">printf</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-string"=
>"%ld\n"</span>, maxofthree(<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-number">-6</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">5</span>));
    <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">printf</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-string"=
>"%ld\n"</span>, maxofthree(<span class=3D"hljs-number">2</span>, <span cla=
ss=3D"hljs-number">4</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">6</span>));
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">=
0</span>;
}
</code></pre>
<pre class=3D"console">$ <kbd>nasm -felf64 maxofthree.asm &amp;&amp; gcc ca=
llmaxofthree.c maxofthree.o &amp;&amp; ./a.out</kbd>
1
2
3
4
5
6
</pre>

<h2>Conditional Instructions</h2>

<p>After an arithmetic or logic instruction, or the compare instruction, <c=
ode>cmp</code>,
the processor sets or clears bits in its <code>rflags</code>. The most inte=
resting flags
are:
</p><ul>
<li><code>s</code> (sign)
</li><li><code>z</code> (zero)
</li><li><code>c</code> (carry)
</li><li><code>o</code> (overflow)
</li></ul>
