<h2>Recursion</h2>

<p>Perhaps surprisingly, there=E2=80=99s nothing out of the ordinary requir=
ed
to implement recursive functions. You just have to be careful to save
registers, as usual. Pushing and popping around the recursive call
is a typical strategy.

</p><div class=3D"filename"><span>factorial.asm</span></div><pre><code clas=
s=3D"language-x86asm hljs" data-highlighted=3D"yes"><span class=3D"hljs-com=
ment">; -------------------------------------------------------------------=
---------</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; An implementation of the recursive function:=
</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;   uint64_t factorial(uint64_t n) {</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;       return (n &lt;=3D 1) ? 1 : n * factori=
al(n-1);</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">;   }</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; --------------------------------------------=
--------------------------------</span>

        <span class=3D"hljs-meta">global</span>  factorial

        <span class=3D"hljs-meta">section</span> .text
<span class=3D"hljs-symbol">factorial:</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">cmp</span>     <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rdi</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>                  <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-comment">; n &lt;=3D 1?</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">jnbe</span>    L1                     =
 <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; if not, go do a recursive call</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">mov</span>     <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-number">1</span>                  <s=
pan class=3D"hljs-comment">; otherwise return 1</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ret</span>
<span class=3D"hljs-symbol">L1:</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">push</span>    <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rdi</span>                     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; save n=
 on stack (also aligns %rsp!)</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">dec</span>     <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rdi</span>                     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; n-1</s=
pan>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">call</span>    factorial              =
 <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; factorial(n-1), result goes in %rax</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">pop</span>     <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rdi</span>                     <span class=3D"hljs-comment">; restor=
e n</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">imul</span>    <span class=3D"hljs-bui=
lt_in">rax</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">rdi</span>                =
<span class=3D"hljs-comment">; n * factorial(n-1), stored in %rax</span>
        <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">ret</span>
</code></pre>
<p>An example caller:

</p><div class=3D"filename"><span>callfactorial.c</span></div><pre><code cl=
ass=3D"language-c hljs" data-highlighted=3D"yes"><span class=3D"hljs-commen=
t">/*
 * An application that illustrates calling the factorial function defined e=
lsewhere.
 */</span>

<span class=3D"hljs-meta">#<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">include</span> <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span>
<span class=3D"hljs-meta">#<span class=3D"hljs-keyword">include</span> <spa=
n class=3D"hljs-string">&lt;inttypes.h&gt;</span></span>

<span class=3D"hljs-type">uint64_t</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title functio=
n_">factorial</span><span class=3D"hljs-params">(<span class=3D"hljs-type">=
uint64_t</span> n)</span>;

<span class=3D"hljs-type">int</span> <span class=3D"hljs-title function_">m=
ain</span><span class=3D"hljs-params">()</span> {
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">for</span> (<span class=3D"hljs-type">uint=
64_t</span> i =3D <span class=3D"hljs-number">0</span>; i &lt; <span class=
=3D"hljs-number">20</span>; i++) {
        <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">printf</span>(<span class=3D"hljs-str=
ing">"factorial(%2lu) =3D %lu\n"</span>, i, factorial(i));
    }
    <span class=3D"hljs-keyword">return</span> <span class=3D"hljs-number">=
0</span>;
}
