<h2>Local Variables and Stack Frames</h2>

<p>First, please read <a href=3D"http://eli.thegreenplace.net/2011/09/06/st=
ack-frame-layout-on-x86-64/">Eli
Bendersky=E2=80=99s article</a>. That overview is more complete than my bri=
ef notes.

</p><p>When a function is called the caller will first put the parameters i=
n the correct registers then issue the <code>call</code> instruction. Addit=
ional parameters beyond those covered by the registers will be pushed on th=
e stack prior to the call. The call instruction puts the return address on =
the top of stack. So if you have the function:

</p><pre class=3D"prettyprint"><span class=3D"pln">int64_t example</span><s=
pan class=3D"pun">(</span><span class=3D"pln">int64_t x</span><span class=
=3D"pun">,</span><span class=3D"pln"> int64_t y</span><span class=3D"pun">)=
</span><span class=3D"pln"> </span><span class=3D"pun">{</span><span class=
=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; int64_t a</span><span class=3D"pun">,</span><spa=
n class=3D"pln"> b</span><span class=3D"pun">,</span><span class=3D"pln"> c=
</span><span class=3D"pun">;</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; b =
</span><span class=3D"pun">=3D</span><span class=3D"pln"> </span><span clas=
s=3D"lit">7</span><span class=3D"pun">;</span><span class=3D"pln"><br>&nbsp=
; &nbsp; </span><span class=3D"kwd">return</span><span class=3D"pln"> x </s=
pan><span class=3D"pun">*</span><span class=3D"pln"> b </span><span class=
=3D"pun">+</span><span class=3D"pln"> y</span><span class=3D"pun">;</span><=
span class=3D"pln"><br></span><span class=3D"pun">}</span></pre>

<p>Then on entry to the function, <mjx-container class=3D"MathJax CtxtMenu_=
Attached_0" jax=3D"SVG" tabindex=3D"0" ctxtmenu_counter=3D"62" style=3D"pos=
ition: relative;"><svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width=3D"1.294e=
x" height=3D"1.025ex" role=3D"img" focusable=3D"false" viewBox=3D"0 -442 57=
2 453" xmlns:xlink=3D"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" aria-hidden=3D"true" st=
yle=3D"vertical-align: -0.025ex;"><g stroke=3D"currentColor" fill=3D"curren=
tColor" stroke-width=3D"0" transform=3D"scale(1,-1)"><g data-mml-node=3D"ma=
th"><g data-mml-node=3D"mi"><use data-c=3D"1D465" xlink:href=3D"#MJX-TEX-I-=
1D465"></use></g></g></g></svg><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=3D"on" displ=
ay=3D"inline"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mi>x</mi>=
</math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> will be in edi, <mjx-container =
class=3D"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0" jax=3D"SVG" tabindex=3D"0" ctxtmenu_c=
ounter=3D"63" style=3D"position: relative;"><svg xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org=
/2000/svg" width=3D"1.109ex" height=3D"1.464ex" role=3D"img" focusable=3D"f=
alse" viewBox=3D"0 -442 490 647" xmlns:xlink=3D"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlin=
k" aria-hidden=3D"true" style=3D"vertical-align: -0.464ex;"><g stroke=3D"cu=
rrentColor" fill=3D"currentColor" stroke-width=3D"0" transform=3D"scale(1,-=
1)"><g data-mml-node=3D"math"><g data-mml-node=3D"mi"><use data-c=3D"1D466"=
 xlink:href=3D"#MJX-TEX-I-1D466"></use></g></g></g></svg><mjx-assistive-mml=
 unselectable=3D"on" display=3D"inline"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/19=
98/Math/MathML"><mi>y</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> will =
be in esi, and the return address will be on the top of the stack. Where ca=
n we put the local variables?  An easy choice is on the stack itself, thoug=
h if you have enough regsters, use them! Registers tend to be faster anyway=
.

</p><p>If you are running on a machine that respect the standard ABI, you c=
an leave rsp where it is and access the =E2=80=9Cextra parameters=E2=80=9D =
and the local variables directly from rsp for example:

</p><div class=3D"memory-view">
<div>rsp-24</div><div>a</div>
<div>rsp-16</div><div>b</div>
<div>rsp-8</div><div>c</div>
<div>rsp</div><div>retaddr</div>
<div>rsp+8</div><div>caller=E2=80=99s<br>stack<br>frame</div>
</div>

<p>So our function looks like this:
</p><pre class=3D"prettyprint lang-asm"><span class=3D"pln">&nbsp; &nbsp; &=
